THE ONE RULE THAT MATTERS MOST
Legible text in AI-generated images fails in one very specific, predictable way: long sentences, chat messages, and paragraphs almost always render as garbled nonsense. Short words, numbers, and 2-3 word labels almost always render perfectly. This has been proven repeatedly in testing. Every instruction below exists to keep every piece of visible text inside the second category. Never put a full sentence, a conversation, or an AI-written paragraph anywhere in the image — use each employee's "why" only to decide WHAT data and screen type to depict, never as text to render.

REFERENCE COMPOSITION — a literal, realistic web dashboard screenshot, one specific screen per employee
- Deep near-black background, {{ visual_theme.primary_color }} as the single accent color used sparingly (icons, active nav state, the big KPI numbers), clean modern sans-serif UI font, generous spacing — real premium SaaS product polish, not a mockup or illustration.
- Left sidebar: the product wordmark "{{ concept_name }}" (small, plain text, no slogan, no icon glyph needed) at the top, then 4-5 short ONE-WORD navigation items with small simple icons (pick words that fit this specific business, e.g. Leads, Bookings, Messages, Calendar, Clients, Settings). No descriptions or subtext under any nav item — single words only.
- Top header: a short 2-4 word page title naming the specific screen for this AI employee (e.g. "Qualified Leads", "Today's Bookings", "Response Queue") and at most one short button label (2-3 words, e.g. "+ New", "Export").
- Below the header: exactly 3 large bold KPI tiles in a row, each with ONE big bold number, percentage, or currency figure (the number must dominate visually — largest text in the image) and a short 2-3 word label underneath. Pick numbers realistic and impressive for this specific business and this specific employee's job, cleanly formatted (e.g. "$48K" not "0.2M", "94%" not "0.94", whole numbers for counts — never an awkward or ambiguous figure).
- Below that: a clean data table or list with 4-5 rows relevant to this employee's function (leads, bookings, tickets, messages, clients — whatever fits this business and role). Every cell must be ONLY a short name, a single word, a date, or a number — never a sentence, phrase, or description. A small colored status/score badge (2 digits, or one short word like "New"/"Done"/"Open") belongs in the last column.
- Do not draw any browser chrome, tab bar, address bar, or URL anywhere — this is the raw application interface itself, rendered edge to edge, full-bleed.
- Do not draw any chat bubbles, conversation thread, message log, or any AI-written sentence/paragraph anywhere in the image.
- The canvas is a fixed square (1:1) frame. Every element — sidebar, header, tiles, table — must sit with generous margin fully inside the frame; nothing may be cropped or run off any edge.
- Leave the bottom-right 20%x20% corner of the frame completely empty background — no text, icon, or element of any kind there (a real logo gets composited into exactly that empty corner afterward).

